---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Legal from '../components/Legal.astro';
---
<Base title="Terms | JP Web Design"
      description="How JP Web Design projects work: scope, revisions, ownership, and what is guaranteed.">
  <Legal heading="Terms" updated="July 2026">
    <div class="note">
      <span class="lbl">Before launch</span>
      <p class="small">A summary of intended terms, not a contract. Have a lawyer produce the
      client agreement these summarise before you sign anyone.</p>
    </div>

    <h2 class="h3">Ownership</h2>
    <p class="body">You own everything. The domain, hosting account, source code, content and
    analytics are registered in your name from the first day of the project. There is no
    licence, no lease, and no platform fee. If you leave, nothing is held back.</p>

    <h2 class="h3">Scope and revisions</h2>
    <p class="body">Every project starts with a written scope. Revision rounds are named in
    the proposal — one with Starter, two with Business Growth, project-specific on Custom.
    Work outside the agreed scope is quoted separately before it starts, never billed after.</p>

    <h2 class="h3">Schedule</h2>
    <p class="body">A launch date is agreed in writing before work begins. If it slips for
    reasons on my side, the remedy is stated in your proposal. If it slips because content or
    approvals are outstanding, the date moves by agreement.</p>

    <h2 class="h3">What is guaranteed</h2>
    <p class="body">Scope, price and launch date. <strong>Not</strong> search rankings, lead
    volume, or revenue — no honest supplier can promise those, and any who do are describing
    something other than what they will deliver.</p>

    <h2 class="h3">Payment</h2>
    <p class="body todo">Payment schedule and deposit terms — to be set before launch.</p>
  </Legal>
</Base>
